ABSTRACT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

We construct the BRST quantization of the Hodge Complex Standard Model (HCSM)
directly on the finite substrate Lambda = Z_8 x Z_8. The substrate's only
nilpotent operator is the Hodge-Dirac operator D = d + d*, satisfying
D^2 = Delta exactly on each form degree. We prove that the substrate's physical
state space is ker D, of dimension 4, and that this dimension is the emergent
spacetime dimension d = 4. The bosonic (Omega^0 + Omega^2) and fermionic
(Omega^1) sectors of the Hodge complex have equal dimension 128, and D swaps
them exactly; this equality is the substrate's native implementation of the
ghost cancellation of continuum BRST, requiring no separate ghost fields.
We prove that the naive lattice BRST operator with the discrete derivative is
NOT nilpotent; its failure is exactly the mixed second derivative
L_1^x L_1^y (c^b c^c) of the ghost bilinear, which is a structural consequence
of the lattice derivative not being a derivation of the Grassmann algebra. We
prove that the diagonal flip F distinguishes the B_1 from the B_2 isotypic
sector of the 14-mode multiplet, making the identification of B_1 with weak
isospin a theorem rather than a labeling convention. We close the partition
function identity by showing Z_gf = lim_{beta -> infinity} Z_sub(beta)
= dim ker D = 4. The framework has zero empirical anchors in this sector.

