--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1.1 Context

The Hodge Complex Standard Model (HCSM) derives the gauge structure, matter
content, and low-energy physics of the Standard Model from a single discrete
substrate: the periodic torus Lambda = Z_8 x Z_8 [1, 2]. The gauge algebra
g_SM = su(3)_c + su(2)_L + u(1)_Y is realized as a Lie subalgebra of the D_4
commutant on the 14-mode multiplet at the self-paired eigenvalue lambda = 4
[6, 7]. The Hodge-Dirac operator D = d + d* satisfies D^2 = Delta on each form
degree [3], and its kernel carries the Lorentzian signature (3,1) that becomes
the emergent spacetime [4, 5].

The classical limits of the framework have been established [15-19]. The Dirac
equation was derived in [19]. Direct quantization of the Hodge complex was
established in [20]. The present paper addresses the BRST structure of the
gauge sector.

