8. THE 2D-TO-4D GAUGE LIFT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

8.1 The Tensor Product Structure

    V_56 = V_14 (x) ker D, with 14 * 4 = 56.

8.2 Lift Construction

The 2D lattice tangent space is the D_4 irrep E (2-dimensional). The 4D kernel
tangent space is 2 A_1 + E. The lift maps

    A_1^a(x)               -> A_1^a(X)                 [transverse]
    A_2^a(x)               -> A_2^a(X)                 [transverse]
    A_1^a(x) + A_2^a(x)    -> sqrt(2) A_3^a(X)         [longitudinal]
    A_1^a(x) - A_2^a(x)    -> sqrt(2) A_0^a(X)         [timelike]

Theorem 8.1 (Uniqueness of Lift). The 2D-to-4D gauge field lift is unique up
to overall scale, given (i) D_4-equivariance, (ii) preservation of the 1-form
structure, (iii) compatibility with the Hodge star on ker D.

Proof. The lattice tangent space is the irreducible E rep. The 4D target is
2 A_1 + E. The E -> E map is unique up to scale. The E -> 2 A_1 map requires
the D_4-invariant norm, which is unique. The Hodge star constraint fixes the
scale.

