11. CONCLUSION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The substrate's BRST structure is D = d + d*, not the imported continuum BRST
operator. The physical state space is ker D, of dimension 4, which is the
emergent spacetime dimension. The bosonic and fermionic sectors of the Hodge
complex have equal dimension 128, and D swaps them exactly; this is the
substrate's native ghost cancellation, requiring no separate ghost fields. The
naive lattice BRST fails in a specific, structural way - the mixed second
derivative L_1^x L_1^y (c^b c^c) - reflecting the lattice derivative not being
a derivation of the Grassmann algebra. The diagonal flip F distinguishes B_1
from B_2, making weak isospin selection a theorem. The partition function
identity is Z_gf = lim_{beta -> infinity} Z_sub(beta) = dim ker D = 4.

The framework's claim is that the Standard Model is what the substrate looks
like when observed. Physics is what the machine cannot cancel. The Hodge
complex is the machine. The kernel is what the machine cannot cancel.

